-- title:
--   Interior order comparison from integrality of X⁶ j^{4m}(j-1728)^{3m}
-- statement:
--   Fix a level $N$, a weight $k \in \mathbb{Z}$ and an integer $m \ge 1$, let $g$ and $h$ be modular forms of weight $k$ for $\Gamma_0(N)$, and let $X$ be a Laurent series over $\mathbb{C}$. Assume first that $X$ times the $q$-expansion of $h$ of width $1$, viewed as a Laurent series, equals the corresponding $q$-expansion of $g$. Write $J =$ `coeffEmb ℂ jq` for the image in `LaurentSeries ℂ` of the rational Laurent series `jq` $=$ `single (-1) 1` $\cdot$ `ofPowerSeries jNumQ` (that is, $q^{-1}$ times the rational power series obtained from the integral series `jNum` by base change) under the coefficientwise ring homomorphism induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to \mathbb{C}$. Assume second that $X^6 \, J^{4m} \, (J - 1728)^{3m}$ is integral over the $\mathbb{C}$-subalgebra of `LaurentSeries ℂ` generated by $J$. Then for every $\tau$ in the upper half-plane, the analytic order at the point $\tau \in \mathbb{C}$ of the function $z \mapsto h(z)\,\Delta(z)^m$, precomposed with `UpperHalfPlane.ofComplex`, is at most the analytic order at $\tau$ of $z \mapsto g(z)\,(E_4(z)^2 E_6(z))^m$, precomposed with `UpperHalfPlane.ofComplex`.
--
--   This is the weight-$2m$ form of the interior (non-cuspidal) half of the analytic criterion comparing the vanishing orders of $h\Delta^m$ and $g(E_4^2E_6)^m$ on $\mathfrak{H}$, the input being integrality over $\mathbb{C}[j]$ of the Laurent series $X^6 j^{4m}(j-1728)^{3m}$ attached to the ratio $X = \tilde g/\tilde h$. It feeds the existence statements [`ModularCurve.exists_cuspForm_qExpansion_eq_mul_thetaL_pow_of_isIntegral`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_cuspForm_qExpansion_eq_mul_thetaL_pow_of_isIntegral) and [`ModularCurve.exists_modularForm_qExpansion_eq_mul_thetaL_pow_of_isIntegral`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_modularForm_qExpansion_eq_mul_thetaL_pow_of_isIntegral), where a $q$-expansion satisfying such an integrality condition is realised by an actual (cusp) form.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_analyticOrderAt_le_of_isIntegral_adjoin_coeffEmb_jq_pow.lean

